      "content": "Leadership in Nursing"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "1n42xkf",
      "content": "Leadership is the ability to guide individuals or groups toward achieving goals. Nurse leaders play an important role in coordinating healthcare teams and ensuring quality patient care."
    },
    {
      "id": "073sgje",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Leadership Style</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Characteristics</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Autocratic leadership</p>",
            "<p>Leader makes decisions without group input</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Democratic leadership</p>",
            "<p>Group members participate in decision‑making</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Laissez‑faire leadership</p>",
            "<p>Leader provides minimal direction</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Transformational leadership</p>",
            "<p>Leader motivates staff through inspiration</p>"
          ]
