    {
      "id": "v1gp6c5",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Nursing Education"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Luther Gulick coined the acronym POSDCORB for management functions; frequently asked in nursing officer competitive exams.",
        "As per INC guidelines, the nurse-patient ratio for ICUs is strictly 1:1 per shift, while high-dependency units require 1:2.",
        "Donabedian's Model categorizes quality assurance into Structure (resources/staff), Process (care delivery), and Outcome (patient satisfaction/recovery).",
        "Unity of Command dictates that an employee should receive orders from only one direct supervisor to prevent role confusion."
      ],
      "id": "q611ztl"
    },
